...A woman is holding me.
Mother.

Facing Mother, one man is there.
—Father.

To Father, Mother speaks. Each word goes in like a point.

&quot;You are not her father.&quot;

Mother says it.

&quot;You must not think yourself this child&#x27;s father.&quot;

&quot;This child is my daughter. Mine alone.&quot;

&quot;This child has no father.&quot;

&quot;This child is not your daughter.&quot;

Father listens. No answer.

From his face, I know. Choosing is not in his hands.
Only the decision is being given to him.

Mother says it again.

&quot;This child has no father.&quot;

—No father for me.

&quot;You are not this child&#x27;s father.&quot;

—This man is not my father.

&quot;This child...<span class="beat" aria-label="Pause">◆</span>you must not love her.&quot;

Then I—
From this man, I will have no love.
